{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/939969-in-a-haywire-town","id":939969,"title":"In a Haywire Town","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-29T23:04:03-07:00","id":939969,"title":"In a Haywire Town","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You know, 2e Mages have a <i>much</i> higher spell control limit than 1e Mages. Prime 3 is <i>devastatingly</i> good at giving you more spell control slots.<br /> <br /> Stealing Fire (Prime 3) lets you turn someone into a Sleepwalker. You can then use a Prime 2 spell through Creative Spellcasting that would give your friend dots in Banner-Bearer equal to Potency. Let's call the latter &quot;Shieldmaiden's Boon&quot;.<br /> <br /> Make sure you have <i>at least</i> Medium Sympathy to them, cast Stealing Fire then Shieldmaiden's Boon at Potency 2. Transfer spell control over to them, and you have a Sleepwalker with one or two open spell control slots. Make both spells lasting, and be happy!<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> The idea of a Mage who has turned <i>everyone</i> in his tiny home town into Sleepwalkers so that he doesn't have to worry about hiding his magic around his friends is interesting.<br /> <br /> <i>Especially</i> after he dies, and literally <i>hundreds</i> of spells start malfunctioning in a town where a good part of the populace suddenly suffers a bajillion Breaking Points and loses the memory of large portions of the last decade or so.<br /> <br /> Man, I want to play one of the Guardians that goes in to clean up <i>that</i> mess... </div> </div> </div>So... yeah. What kind of whacky, spooky stuff would you find in the aftermath of a town where a (recently deceased) Mage has turned all thousand or so residents into Sleepwalkers... and has used as many of them as possible for spell control? And how did he pull this off in the first place? <div align=\"center\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Welcome to Little Atlantis, A Wonderful Place To Live.&quot;</span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T02:12:04-07:00","id":940012,"title":"","content":"This is brilliant. Very excited to see where this goes, other than horribly wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T06:07:25-07:00","id":940061,"title":"","content":"As to how to pull it off, cast Stealing Fire with a large number of targets then offload maintenance onto one of them, for safety keep track of these groups and have a couple redundant spells offloaded onto different people in the group.<br /> <br /> That is, say he is casting with 20 targets per casting, he keeps track of the list of people effected by each casting, and casts it on them again, off loading one copy of the spell onto one person in the group, and offloading the other onto another person in the group who doesn't generally spend time near the first.<br /> <br /> This way if someone accidentally dies a bunch of people don't suddenly have their minds implode from breaking points. When one of the people carrying a Stealing Fire Spell dies he just casts it on their group again and offloads it onto someone else in the group.<br /> <br /> This leaves a large number of sleepwalkers to carry other spells.<br /> <br /> Edit: This also means there is probably a ledger and a log somewhere with a bunch of info necessary to maintain this system and minimize risks. &quot;Bob has become friends with Alice, need to move the fire from Alice to Charlie. Can't risk both bearers in their group dying in a car crash together!&quot; Imagine someone finding these without context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11888,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","user":"Custos Tenebrarum","date":". 07-30-2016, 09:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T08:31:48-07:00","id":940089,"title":"","content":"This is both so awesome and so wrong that my head may explode from the paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6770-midgardener","name":"Midgardener","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6770_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T08:50:36-07:00","id":940095,"title":"","content":"This is a delightful idea and an even greater Mystery to throw in. Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T19:27:27-07:00","id":940391,"title":"","content":"Build a legacy around doing this to everyone in the world. If any other mage dispels your Stealing Fire and the victim turns into a dribbling vegetable, tell everyone that it was the mage's fault, and get them to organize a witch hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T08:38:59-07:00","id":940629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/939969-in-a-haywire-town?p=940391#post940391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Build a legacy around doing this to everyone in the world. If any other mage dispels your Stealing Fire and the victim turns into a dribbling vegetable, tell everyone that it was the mage's fault, and get them to organize a witch hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>I started making a legacy like that a little while ago but then went in a different direction.<br /> <br /> Their fifth attainment would have been based off Stealing Fire with two Reaches and one of the two additional Spell Factor increases (from the imaginary 5 dice due to its dots) on Indefinite Duration, the last Reach would be spent on Instant Casting, and the other Spell Factor increase would be spent on Area.<br /> <br /> The book says that the Attainments have effective Successes equal to Dots, and since it is a fifth Attainment that's 5 successes which is an Exceptional Success which means it can ignore Withstand.<br /> <br /> This means that every time they use this Attainment (which costs 1 Mana due to Indefinite) everyone in a small room is now permanently a Sleepwalker because Indefinite Duration Legacy Attainments are pretty much Lasting because they count as natural phenomena.<br /> <br /> Anyone with the fifth Attainment in a Prime based Legacy is going to have a ton of Mana so the elders of the Legacy spend all their excess Mana on using this Attainment on sections of crowds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11888-custos-tenebrarum","name":"Custos Tenebrarum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T21:45:27-07:00","id":941032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Custos Tenebrarum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/939969-in-a-haywire-town?p=940629#post940629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I started making a legacy like that a little while ago but then went in a different direction.<br /> <br /> Their fifth attainment would have been based off Stealing Fire with two Reaches and one of the two additional Spell Factor increases (from the imaginary 5 dice due to its dots) on Indefinite Duration, the last Reach would be spent on Instant Casting, and the other Spell Factor increase would be spent on Area.<br /> <br /> The book says that the Attainments have effective Successes equal to Dots, and since it is a fifth Attainment that's 5 successes which is an Exceptional Success which means it can ignore Withstand.<br /> <br /> This means that every time they use this Attainment (which costs 1 Mana due to Indefinite) everyone in a small room is now permanently a Sleepwalker because Indefinite Duration Legacy Attainments are pretty much Lasting because they count as natural phenomena.<br /> <br /> Anyone with the fifth Attainment in a Prime based Legacy is going to have a ton of Mana so the elders of the Legacy spend all their excess Mana on using this Attainment on sections of crowds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm.... I really like the idea, but it explicitly contradicts the canon idea that mages cannot create sleepwalkers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T01:19:03-07:00","id":941094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/939969-in-a-haywire-town?p=941032#post941032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm.... I really like the idea, but it explicitly contradicts the canon idea that mages cannot create sleepwalkers.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, although I see it as a possibility for a story that would essentially be about a &quot;Hieromagus Legacy&quot;. A mage needs to go through certain ordeals to forge his soul into a Legacy and mages can't just decide to destroy the Lie, so this would be heavily affected by a storyteller fiat (maybe things like never overreaching and risking a Paradox before entering the Legacy, among other things).<br /> <br /> But hey, that's why the Hieromagus is mentioned in the lore at all, so that the players have a chance to become one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T04:04:42-07:00","id":941129,"title":"","content":"I'd like to add, that you can only load spells onto sleepwalkers if they willingly accept this. So besides making a whole town full of sleepwalkers the mage doing this would probably need to form some kind of cult, so that every member accepts him as their leader and willingly does everything the mage wants. A whole cult of sleepwalkers is pretty terrifiying even without the mage loading spells on those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T06:49:54-07:00","id":941162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/939969-in-a-haywire-town?p=941129#post941129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to add, that you can only load spells onto sleepwalkers if they willingly accept this. So besides making a whole town full of sleepwalkers the mage doing this would probably need to form some kind of cult, so that every member accepts him as their leader and willingly does everything the mage wants. A whole cult of sleepwalkers is pretty terrifiying even without the mage loading spells on those.</div> </div> </div> </div>They also have to have at least a Medium connection to hold the spells in the first place.<br /> <br /> Which makes the place <i>even more frightening</i> now that the guy's dead.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}